I guess it's personal peference (therefore I said
"*maybe* prettier" upthread), but all that <tag>,
</tag> clutters the source, IMO. It's not that bad
to write  "<b>text</b>"  instead of  ".B text"  but
I think the former is less legible. Yet much more
illegible if you consider  ".I text"  compared to
the HTML/CSS overhead to define "font-style:italic"
or add class attributes to a tag. Shudder. (Okay,
there's also the  "<em>text</em>"  etc., granted.)

I've done quite some HTML in the past two years and
must say that the inconsistencies in the language,
e.g. WRT applicability of attributes, is a horror.
So I'd attribute the "hodgepodge" equally to HTML.

